      "writtenOn": "2026-09-02T19:06:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you referring to CONFIG_PDC_POWER_MGMT_POWER_STATE_DEBOUNCE_PERIOD_MS (originally introduced in crrev.com/c/5770775 and made configurable in crrev.com/c/7075756), which handles coalescing rapid S0/suspend bouncing?\n\nThis CL fixes a separate intra-handler issue: once pdc_apply_power_state_policy() actually executes for S0, it was calling startup_policy_1 (forcing Sink-only) immediately followed by resume_policy_2 (restoring DRP). Replacing startup_policy_1 with direct S0 notification keeps the retimer enabled without flapping port roles.",
